From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 19:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: attach PPE on immediate vdev start

The delayed station-vdev path attaches its direct-switch virtual port,
but the normal channel-assignment path did not.  AP vdevs normally take
the latter path, leaving them without a PPE VP even though all rings were
running.  Attach the VP after a successful immediate vdev start and roll
the vdev back if the attachment fails.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -11555,6 +11555,14 @@ ath12k_mac_op_assign_vif_chanctx(struct
 	}
 
 	arvif->is_started = true;
+	ret = ath12k_ppe_ds_vif_attach(arvif);
+	if (ret) {
+		ath12k_warn(ab, "failed to attach vdev %u to PPE: %d\n",
+			    arvif->vdev_id, ret);
+		ath12k_mac_vdev_stop(arvif);
+		arvif->is_started = false;
+		goto out;
+	}
 
 	/* TODO: Setup ps and cts/rts protection */
 
